      "summary": "Composed in Greek, most likely between about 70 and 90 CE, probably in or near Syria. The earliest surviving pieces are small papyrus fragments from Egypt copied within roughly a century of composition. The earliest complete copy is in Codex Sinaiticus, a parchment book of about 330–360 CE found at Saint Catherine's Monastery at the foot of Mount Sinai and brought to scholarly attention between 1844 and 1859; Codex Vaticanus, of about the same date, preserves it as well. The original, like all books of its time, ran as continuous text with no chapter or verse numbers. The Greek printed here follows a modern critical edition assembled from these earliest witnesses.",
